description:
The singleton interface lacks some flexibility and it causes periodic problems with CPPR testing.  If more than one CPPR server is running under the same user, even though they use different directories, the singleton file will always be the same.

I propose making the following changes
1. Remove the flags from crt_init.
2. Add an API, something like the following:
/* If crt is initialized, write out attach information to a file.   If filename isn't NULL, generate a unique filename and return the name.  If it is NULL, a filename is created using old behavior based on the server name.   The server application can make this filename available to clients.   If called more than once, it can just return the filename.
*/
int crt_allow_singleton(const char **filename);

/* Attach a singleton to the server described in filename.  If filename is NULL, it defaults to old behavior based on group id */
int crt_group_attach_singleton(crt_group_id_t srv_id, const char *filename, crt_group_t **attached_grp);

If the singleton is created, it is unlinked on crt_finalize.   

The CNSS has a mechanism for exporting information (such as this filename) to users so this gives us flexibility we need.

