description:
Currently the protobuf definition of the NVMe health stats structure is very different from the structure returned by our SPDK binding as well as the native structure defined in the storage package.

Current:
{noformat}
        message Health {
                uint32 temp = 1;
                uint32 tempwarn = 2; // temperature warning duration
                uint32 tempcrit = 3; // temperature critical duration
                uint64 ctrlbusy = 4; // controller busy duration
                uint64 powercycles = 5;
                uint64 poweronhours = 6;
                uint64 unsafeshutdowns = 7;
                uint64 mediaerrors = 8;
                uint64 errorlogs = 9; // error log entries
                // critical warnings
                bool tempwarning = 10;
                bool availspare = 11;
                bool reliability = 12;
                bool readonly = 13;
                bool volatilemem = 14;
        }
{noformat}

The intent was probably to make these fields convenient/easy to remember, but the end result is that converting between types (as is necessary at package/network boundaries) is a manual process.

I propose that we modify the protobuf definition to match the SPDK/native structures, which look like the following:

{noformat}
        NvmeDeviceHealth struct {
                Temp            uint32
                TempWarnTime    uint32
                TempCritTime    uint32
                CtrlBusyTime    uint64
                PowerCycles     uint64
                PowerOnHours    uint64
                UnsafeShutdowns uint64
                MediaErrors     uint64
                ErrorLogEntries uint64
                TempWarn        bool
                AvailSpareWarn  bool
                ReliabilityWarn bool
                ReadOnlyWarn    bool
                VolatileWarn    bool
                CtrlrPciAddr    string
        }
{noformat}

I'd like to do this ASAP as it's making my refactor of the bdev code more difficult than necessary.

