description:
In order to better exercise the metadata operations and conditional update logic we need to add a test suite that runs the tests associated with the daos_test -F parameter in parallel ideally over multiple client nodes.

so something like:
{code:java}
mpirun -np 16 --hostfile xyz daos_test -F{code}

The new interface proposal: defer all parsing and setting bits to gurt and not cart/daos.

 int d_log_dbg_bit_alloc(const char name, int bit);

int d_log_dbg_group_alloc(const char *grp_name, int mask); -----if user defines some bits and wants to add an identifier for a group of them

And go back to previous function definition with no parameters: d_log_sync_mask(void) - which will re-read environment to make sure all the appropriate bits are set.

Just to clarify a bit more no the proposed interface, suppose we have the following bits cat, mouse, dog, tree, flower And groups plant, animal

User would do the following:

d_log_dbg_bit_alloc("cat", &cat);

d_log_dbg_bit_alloc("dog", &dog);

d_log_dbg_bit_alloc("mouse", &mouse);

d_log_dbg_group_alloc("animal", cat | dog | mouse);

d_log_dbg_bit_alloc("tree", &tree);

d_log_dbg_bit_alloc("flower", &flower);

d_log_dbg_group_alloc("plant", flower | tree);

d_log_sync_masks();

So, if user set DD_MASK=animal they would get cat, dog, and mouse streams Other components would do similar The parser would need to skip as of yet undefined items like it does today with CRT_LOG_MASK

